<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kidara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 4th–5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Kidara I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kidara was the founder of the Kidarite kingdom, who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and later Gandhara around the late 4th and early 5th centuries CE. Known mainly from coins, which bear his name and copy Kushan and Sasanian designs, he claimed the old Kushan royal title and gave his name to the dynasty, which fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> and later threatened Gupta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kidara.jpg" alt="Kidara" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins. Contoured by myself पाटलिपुत्र (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kidara_I_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
